**Example Apparatus Claim**

1. A torch comprising:  
   a housing;  
   a light source disposed within the housing and configured to emit light along an optical path;  
   a first condenser lens group positioned along the optical path and configured to collect and condense light emitted by the light source;  
   an optical filter positioned downstream of the first condenser lens group and configured to diffuse the condensed light, thereby promoting a substantially uniform light-intensity distribution; and  
   a second condenser lens group positioned downstream of the optical filter and configured to condense the diffused light into a concentrated, substantially uniform circular illumination beam.

**Example Method Claim**

2. A method of producing an illumination beam with a torch, the method comprising:  
   emitting light from a light source;  
   condensing the emitted light using a first condenser lens group;  
   passing the condensed light through an optical filter to diffuse the light and increase spatial uniformity thereof; and  
   condensing the diffused light using a second condenser lens group to form a concentrated, substantially uniform circular illumination beam.
